Tier 1 -- pure unit tests (workstation, milliseconds).

The policy functions, kept out of the verbs so they are testable without a
system: snapshot-name parse/format/compare, staleness arithmetic, succession
resolution, quorum evaluation, retention-ladder selection. Table-driven, no
ZFS, no jails, no CBSD. See TESTING.md §2.

At M0 this tier holds only the harness's own self-test: proof that a failing
assertion is reported as "not ok" and exits non-zero.

Files named t_*.sh are tests. Anything else here (this README, future fixture
data) is ignored by tests/run.sh.

Since M3 this tier also holds the tier-7 simulator's own units, which need no
cluster: t_sim_gen.sh (the seeded PRNG and weighted chooser -- determinism,
weights, and drawing only from what was offered) and t_sim_shrink.sh (prefix
bisection and event-kind removal, driven by an injected fake rerun function).

Since M5, t_setup_headless.sh: `seance setup`'s --set/--answers/--from path,
which is also the only path this tier can exercise -- the interactive
bsddialog wizard needs a real terminal, and t_setup_bsddialog_coverage.sh
(tier 3) is what stands in for testing it, by asserting from source that every
screen it could show has exactly this tier's answer-key equivalent.
